meta {
  name: List what is not set up yet
  type: http
  seq: 41
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/organizations/{{organization_id}}/coverage-gaps
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  What is missing between your things, the same list Home suggests from: websites and servers nobody monitors, servers without the agent, no alert channel, domains with auto-renew off or not renewing, mail domains whose DNS nobody checks, zones not linked to their domain, and providers your domains use that you have not connected. Each gap has a `kind`, its `subjects` (`type`, `id`, `label` and the `signals` it was ranked by, best first) and the `fix` that closes it (`action`, and `monitors_each`, what one subject costs against your plan's monitors). A gap is listed only when you may read the module its subjects belong to — domains, servers, DNS or monitoring. `sources` says which kinds were checked: one whose check failed reads `failed`, never "nothing missing". A gap is something not set up yet, never something wrong.

  Scope: `monitoring.read`
}
